# 5b piece 3a — two mutations, never committed, each reverted (both files compared byte-for-byte after)
# command per mutation: swift test --filter AppleSessionEndingTests   (this Mac: macOS 26.6.1, Xcode 27, Swift 6.4)
#
# M6  TurnCoordinator.stop() does not call endConversation()
#     convicted by both AC-310 rows: the session is still held after stop(), and the second conversation's
#     session is reported as .memoryChanged instead of .newConversation.
# M8  SessionKeeper: a failed answer is not let go at once (the ended(...) call removed)
#     convicted by both AC-307 rows: the keeper still holds it, and the next birth says .lastAnswerUnfinished
#     (it only found the session busy) instead of .lastAnswerFailed("the model fell over").
#
# NOT run, and why: raising the ticket inside endConversation() matters only when the conversation ends while
# a NEW session is being made (between the decision and the install). The fake makes sessions synchronously,
# so no row can land an ending in that window; the line is there by the ticket law (§4.1), not by a row.

